notes: V0310 applies the strongest V038/R10 physical camera-tuning evidence to the actual ESP32-CAM production path while preserving PC Studio compatibility. The production ESP uses one framebuffer and selects CAMERA_GRAB_LATEST on PSRAM, retains the existing freshness-first ATL1 length-prefixed TCP JPEG protocol on port 81, and replaces the inherited real sendmsg hot path with bounded plain send operations capped at the R10-winning 11680-byte application write size. TCP_NODELAY, keepalive, progress/deadline limits, complete-frame socket failure semantics, reconnect/session recovery, saved frame-size/JPEG-quality/FPS control, simulation coexistence and all downstream CameraFrameService consumers remain unchanged. V0310 does not force diagnostic JPEG quality 18, does not add the Pi-style cache because R10 showed no matched-target gain, and does not claim the diagnostic 12.43 FPS result until the production ATL1 path is physically retested. The standalone R10 diagnostic firmware remains available for A/B comparison. V039 is the previous unaccepted candidate and V024 / 0_2_4 remains the owner-confirmed passed baseline until explicit owner acceptance changes it.
